---
title: CIBA Step-Up for High-Value Transfer (STEP_UP_METHOD=ciba)
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant B as Browser (UserDashboard)
    participant BFF as BFF (demo_api_server)
    participant TC as tokenChainService.js
    participant P1 as PingOne (bc-authorize)
    participant U as User device (out-of-band)

    %% ── 428 gate — frontend-driven bridge ───────────────────────────────────
    Note over B,P1: STEP_UP_METHOD=ciba — the BFF gate returns 428, it does NOT call cibaService itself
    B->>BFF: POST /api/transactions (transfer >= confirm_threshold_usd)
    BFF-->>B: 428 { step_up_method: 'ciba', step_up_acr }
    Note over B: handleCibaStepUp reacts to the 428

    %% ── initiate ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    B->>BFF: POST /api/auth/ciba/initiate { login_hint, binding_message }
    BFF->>P1: bc-authorize (login_hint, binding_message, scope, acr_values)
    P1-->>BFF: { auth_req_id, expires_in, interval }
    BFF-->>B: { auth_req_id, authReqId, expires_in, interval }
    Note over B,BFF: route returns BOTH casings — tokens never reach the browser

    %% ── out-of-band approval ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    P1->>U: Approval request on the policy-bound channel (email / SMS / FIDO2 / push)
    U-->>P1: User approves

    %% ── poll ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    loop until approved / denied / expired
        B->>BFF: GET /api/auth/ciba/poll/:authReqId
        BFF->>P1: poll token endpoint (auth_req_id)
        alt still pending
            P1-->>BFF: authorization_pending (or slow_down)
            BFF-->>B: { status: 'pending' }
        else approved
            P1-->>BFF: { access_token, id_token, refresh_token }
            BFF->>BFF: store tokens server-side (BFF), stepUpVerified = +5 min
            BFF->>TC: trackTokenEvent(auth, grantedVia: 'ciba')
            BFF-->>B: { status: 'approved' }
        end
    end

    %% ── transfer proceeds ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    B->>BFF: POST /api/transactions (retry)
    BFF-->>B: 200 transaction result
    Note over B,TC: The CIBA Step-Up tab + floating token-chain panel show the backchannel-granted token
